      {
        "id": 46529,
        "name": "Unsafe_Bet",
        "username": "Unsafe_Bet",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/u/53a042/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-09-01T20:35:55.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Pydro\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/48/1844_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Pydro:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The card doesn't apply to an incapped hero (it doesn't have powers or a hand)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>But it very much applies to the remaining heroes, and if \"all players\" have to discard and some can't, the incap heroes basically cause a game loss just by existing.&nbsp; (Hostage Situation works the same way, now that I read it again; somehow I thought they were different.)</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>and only the active heroes have to discard.&nbsp; EDIT: This is how it works on the Mea Computer.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The what?&nbsp; Other than whatever a \"mea computer\" is, do you have any other source to support that only active heroes have to discard?</p>",
