      {
        "id": 46535,
        "name": "grysqrl",
        "username": "grysqrl",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/grysqrl/{size}/1909_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-09-02T00:14:08.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Mega Computer is part of the video game playtesting that strips away the graphical interface and lets you play games through a command line interface (e.g. play card 5; discard cards 2 and 7; hit target 3, then target 4, then in any order after that). It doesn't have a list of rules that you can just read through - the goal is to adjust the internal electronic rules to make them identical to how the game is actually played.</p><p>So, if someone says that it is played a certain way in the Mega Computer, that -may- mean that it is correct, since the Mega Computer is attempting to mimic the actual rules. Alternately, it may be wrong in the Mega Computer and we just haven't caught it yet. In this case, I suspect it is the latter (i.e. I don't think you are completely hosed if one hero is incapped)</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:20:02.693Z",
